!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Embryonic tissues were micro-dissected at E8.5, E10.5 or E11.5 and incubated in trypsin 0.5%/EDTA 1X at 37 °C for 10 minutes and rinsed in DMEM 1X/ FBS 10%. Cranial neural crest cells (CNCCs) were then dissociated with a pipette, filtered and collected by FACS. After sorting, CNCCs were pelleted by centrifugation for 5 minutes, 1000 rpm at 4°C. Total RNA was extracted using PicoPure® Kit (KIT0204 Life Technologies).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For sequencing of total RNA, unstranded RNA-Seq libraries were prepared using the ScriptSeq v2 RNA-Seq Library preparation Kit. Three samples with different barcodes were mixed at equimolar ratios per pool. Sequencing was performed on an Illumina HiSeq 2500 machine (50 bp read length, single-end reads) according to Illumina standards.
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina RTA 1.18.64 and bcl2fastq2 v2.17 was used for basecalling and demultiplexing.
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned to the GRCm38/mm10 reference genome using the QuasR Bioconductor package (PMID: 25417205, version 1.12.0) by the qAlign function with parameters maxHits=10 (allowing up to 10 hits per read, reporting one randomly) and splicedAlignment=TRUE (spiced alignment using SpliceMap PMID: 20371516).
!Sample_data_processing = For each gene, alignments overlapping any of its exons (obtained from Ensemble Release 71) were counted using the QuasR qCount function with default parameters.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCm38/mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Comma-seperated text file with gene annotation (Ensembl identifier, representative transcript, coordinates, strand, gene symbol and biotype, number of exonic bases) and raw alignment counts for each gene and sample.
